    "context": "River regulation and altered flow regimes have profoundly affected estuarine and riverine ecosystems globally, including the Coorong, a Ramsar-listed hypersaline lagoonal system at the terminus of the Murray–Darling Basin (MDB), Australia. Freshwater inflows are critical for regulating salinity and sustaining ecological functions in the Coorong for both the keystone seagrass species and estuarine fish. Quantifying the benefit of environmental water delivery on ecological outcome helps inform decisions to balance environmental and human needs. How does environmental water delivery alter the spatial and temporal distribution of suitable habitat for native fish? Do some species benefit from it more than others?",
